Hairston clearly does not play on a busy, slow, system where it can be hard
to be sure if your keystroke got in or not.  It's real easy to loose track
of that in confirmation sequences, or anything else that's real repetetive
without specific feedback (a changing message is not specific enough for me).

On some systems, it's just too easy to be bitten by the ambiguity of
overloaded characters on overloaded systems.
